      "s": "shuowen_jiezi",
      "t": "筋也。象人筋之形。治功曰力，能圉大災。凡力之屬皆从力。",
      "w": 1
    },
    {
      "s": "wiktionary",
      "t": "Pictogram (象形) – alternative interpretation, either an arm bending out from the side of the body, or a wooden plough. The original version was 𠠲 and the letter ㄌ in zhuyin alphabet was inspired by this character.\nSee also the original version of 爭, in which another plow can be seen. Unrelated to 工 and perhaps to 耒 since they are two different tools. Also unrelated to 另.\nFrom Proto-Sino-Tibetan *k-ra (“strength; to win; classifier for people”) + *-k (STEDT; Schuessler, 2007). Cognate with Burmese အား (a:, “strength; force”); Proto-Loloish *ra² (“strength”), whence Nuosu ꊋ (we); Panyi Bai [script needed] (ɣɯ̱⁴², “strength”); Central Bai hhep (“strength”). A causative derivative is 飭 (OC rhək) (Schuessler, 2007).\nSchuessler (2007) also suggests an etymological connection with 來 (OC *m·rɯːɡ, “to come”)."
    }
  ],
  "shuowen": "筋也。象人筋之形。治功曰力，能圉大災。凡力之屬皆从力。",
